Choose a license for your addon and replace this whole file with its text.

Without a license, other people have no permission to copy, change or share your code.

Common choices for Minecraft mods:

  * MIT or Apache-2.0: anyone may use, change and redistribute the code, also in closed projects.
  * LGPL-3.0-only (what MCHeli: Revived uses) or MPL-2.0: changed copies of your files stay open.
  * All Rights Reserved: you keep every right; others may only download and play.

https://choosealicense.com explains the differences. After choosing, set mod_license in gradle.properties
to the license's SPDX id (for example MIT); it goes into neoforge.mods.toml and fabric.mod.json.

Your content pack may refer to MCHeli's bundled sounds and models by name, as the sample weapon does.
Copying MCHeli's own files into your jar is different: check MCHeli's license first.
